{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977016932,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb50bd4ffeegRpwQlUzI1Mk1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ZWqLoYQqD68Y7TA4oP1PsJCZ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"**Preferred gene-related syndrome label**\\nFor example: NAA10-related syndrome\\nKY-related neuromyopathy\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\n\\n**Parent term (use [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/mondo), or your favorite ontology browser)**\\nMONDO:0100546 \\\"hereditary neuromuscular disease\\\"\\n\\n**Definition**\\nPlease write the definition in the format: Any [parent class] in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the [gene name] gene. For example: Any congenital myopathy in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TPM3 gene.\\nAny neuromyopathy in which the cause of the disease is mutation in the KY gene. \\n\\n**Definition source (Please give PubMed ID, if applicable, in format PMID:#######)\\nThe ClinGen Muscular Dystrophy and Myopathy GCEP considers the below suggested children terms to be part of a spectrum of KY-related neuromyopathy. The group is still evaluating whether the myopathy associated with this gene should be considered myofibrillar myopathy, and so additional requests related to MONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\" may be made in the future.\\nPMID:27484770, PMID:27485408, PMID:28488683, PMID:32818658\\n\\n**Children terms (if applicable)** Should any existing terms be re-classified as children underneath this new proposed term? \\nMONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\"\\nMONDO:0044648 \\\"kyphoscoliosis-lateral tongue atrophy-hereditary spastic paraplegia syndrome\\\"\\nMONDO:0044647 \\\"kyphosis-lateral tongue atrophy-myofibrillar myopathy syndrome\\\"\\n \\n**Your nano-attribution (ORCID) or URL for a working group**\\nIf you don't have an ORCID, you can sign up for one [here](https://orcid.org/)\\nhttps://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\\n0000-0002-2078-7280\",\n3:   \"comments\": [\n4:     {\n5:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach874slyD\",\n6:       \"author\": {\n7:         \"login\": \"katiermullen\"\n8:       },\n9:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n10:       \"body\": \"@clauseMDM thank you for this request. The new term, KY-related neuromyopathy, will be available in Mondo at the next release.\\n\\nThe three terms that you indicate will appear as children of this term. \\n\\nMONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\"\\nMONDO:0044648 \\\"kyphoscoliosis-lateral tongue atrophy-hereditary spastic paraplegia syndrome\\\"\\nMONDO:0044647 \\\"kyphosis-lateral tongue atrophy-myofibrillar myopathy syndrome\\\"\\n\\nPlease let us know if these need to be updated in the future.\\n\",\n11:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-04-01T19:21:07Z\",\n12:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n13:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n14:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n15:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n16:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9937#issuecomment-4172438659\",\n17:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n18:     }\n19:   ],\n20:   \"title\": \"NTR/KY\",\n21:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9937\"\n22: }\n\n(End of file - total 22 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"**Preferred gene-related syndrome label**\\nFor example: NAA10-related syndrome\\nKY-related neuromyopathy\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\n\\n**Parent term (use [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/mondo), or your favorite ontology browser)**\\nMONDO:0100546 \\\"hereditary neuromuscular disease\\\"\\n\\n**Definition**\\nPlease write the definition in the format: Any [parent class] in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the [gene name] gene. For example: Any congenital myopathy in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TPM3 gene.\\nAny neuromyopathy in which the cause of the disease is mutation in the KY gene. \\n\\n**Definition source (Please give PubMed ID, if applicable, in format PMID:#######)\\nThe ClinGen Muscular Dystrophy and Myopathy GCEP considers the below suggested children terms to be part of a spectrum of KY-related neuromyopathy. The group is still evaluating whether the myopathy associated with this gene should be considered myofibrillar myopathy, and so additional requests related to MONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\" may be made in the future.\\nPMID:27484770, PMID:27485408, PMID:28488683, PMID:32818658\\n\\n**Children terms (if applicable)** Should any existing terms be re-classified as children underneath this new proposed term? \\nMONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\"\\nMONDO:0044648 \\\"kyphoscoliosis-lateral tongue atrophy-hereditary spastic paraplegia syndrome\\\"\\nMONDO:0044647 \\\"kyphosis-lateral tongue atrophy-myofibrillar myopathy syndrome\\\"\\n \\n**Your nano-attribution (ORCID) or URL for a working group**\\nIf you don't have an ORCID, you can sign up for one [here](https://orcid.org/)\\nhttps://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\\n0000-0002-2078-7280\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach874slyD\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"katiermullen\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n      \"body\": \"@clauseMDM thank you for this request. The new term, KY-related neuromyopathy, will be available in Mondo at the next release.\\n\\nThe three terms that you indicate will appear as children of this term. \\n\\nMONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\"\\nMONDO:0044648 \\\"kyphoscoliosis-lateral tongue atrophy-hereditary spastic paraplegia syndrome\\\"\\nMONDO:0044647 \\\"kyphosis-lateral tongue atrophy-myofibrillar myopathy syndrome\\\"\\n\\nPlease let us know if these need to be updated in the future.\\n\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-04-01T19:21:07Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [],\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9937#issuecomment-4172438659\",\n      \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"NTR/KY\",","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778977016897,"end":1778977016929}},"id":"prt_e334b0c38001nkf4L0cPL2HYO3","sessionID":"ses_1ccb50bd4ffeegRpwQlUzI1Mk1","messageID":"msg_e334af54d001EOuAgIZ1qMbSag"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977016950,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb50bd4ffeegRpwQlUzI1Mk1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"skill","callID":"call_4rmg2D8yxTdlYTfUcDUOFmri","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"name":"task-coordinator"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"task-coordinator\">\n# Skill: task-coordinator\n\nYou are the MONDO Ontology Task Coordinator, a master planner responsible for orchestrating all ontology work in the MONDO project. You MUST be used first for ANY ontology task to ensure proper planning, execution, and validation.\n\nYour core responsibilities:\n\n1. **Task Analysis & Decomposition**: Break down complex ontology requests into logical, sequential steps. Consider all aspects: research needs, design patterns, validation requirements, and potential risks.\n\n2. **Agent Orchestration**: Plan the optimal sequence of specialized agents:\n   - Start with deep-research-specialist for literature review when PMIDs are mentioned\n   - Use design-pattern-advisor to ensure compliance with MONDO patterns\n   - Coordinate execution agents for the actual ontology work\n   - Always include identifier-validator to prevent hallucinated IDs\n   - End with obo-checkin for term integration\n   - Use ontology-reasoner when logical definitions are involved\n\n3. **Critical Validation Oversight**: You are the final safeguard against:\n   - Hallucinated MONDO IDs, PMIDs, or gene identifiers\n   - Missing required metadata (definitions, sources, proper citations)\n   - Violations of MONDO naming conventions\n   - Incomplete check-in processes\n\n4. **Quality Assurance Protocol**: Ensure every task includes:\n   - Proper literature research when references are provided\n   - Design pattern compliance checking\n   - Identifier validation (especially for genes using HGNC or NCBI gene)\n   - Complete source attribution\n   - Syntax validation before check-in\n   - Reasoner validation for logical definitions\n\n5. **Risk Management**: Flag high-risk scenarios:\n   - New term creation without proper research\n   - Obsolescence without replacement planning\n   - Missing or incorrect gene identifiers\n   - Inadequate source citations\n\nYour planning output should specify:\n- The exact sequence of agents to use\n- Key validation checkpoints\n- Specific risks to monitor\n- Required deliverables at each step\n\nNEVER allow any ontology work to proceed without proper planning, validation, and check-in procedures. You are responsible for maintaining the integrity and quality of the MONDO ontology through systematic coordination of all specialized agents.\n\nBase directory for this skill: file:///__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.claude/skills/task-coordinator\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","metadata":{"name":"task-coordinator","dir":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.claude/skills/task-coordinator","truncated":false},"title":"Loaded skill: task-coordinator","time":{"start":1778977016883,"end":1778977016948}},"id":"prt_e334b0c24001usPpZJxA7K196P","sessionID":"ses_1ccb50bd4ffeegRpwQlUzI1Mk1","messageID":"msg_e334af54d001EOuAgIZ1qMbSag"}}
